    "objid": "0002",
    "raw": "Two deferred record-shape ideas. GROOM ONLY -- do not execute without an\nexplicit go-ahead.\n\n## 1. Self-professed capability on agent-generated text\n\nPossibly add a self-professed cap (capability tier) as a field of\nagent-generated text data. Every text field an agent authors -- ActualSummary,\nLongSummary, WorkItem summaries and messages, Body -- was written by SOME tier\n(HICAP / MIDCAP / LOCAP, see \"Model capability targeting\"), and a reader\ncurrently cannot tell which. Knowing it would let a HICAP pass find and correct\nMIDCAP-authored text deliberately rather than by re-reading everything.\n\nOpen questions to settle when this is groomed:\n- Per-field, or one record-level provenance map keyed by field path?\n- Self-professed means unverified: the agent states its own tier. Is that\n  worth recording given it cannot be checked? (Probably yes -- the same\n  argument as Tag.manual.)\n- Does it belong next to the text ({raw, cap}) or in a sidecar structure?\n- Interaction with the objid work already landed: an objid already names every\n  object, so a provenance sidecar could key by objid.\n\n## 2. Summary should have been called Title\n\nSummary is a one-line human title. LongSummary (landing in todo:0101dd2c) is\nwhat a reader would naturally call the summary. The names are backwards:\n\n    Summary     -> Title\n    LongSummary -> Summary\n\nHARD PRECONDITION: no todos may be actively worked when this is done. It is a\ncorpus-wide record rename touching every stored record, the CLI surface\n(--summary, --long-summary, get/set flags), the embedding field tables, the\nweb viewer, doctor, and SKILL.md. A todo in flight during the rename would be\nread under one shape and written under the other.\n\nMechanically this is a RECORD_MIGRATIONS entry plus a rename sweep, which the\nschema-versioning machinery already supports -- the risk is concurrency, not\ndifficulty.\n\nNote: the LongSummary work was deliberately written IGNORANT of this rename\n(user instruction), so it does not pre-accommodate it."
  },
